<title>JAPAN: Tosok bid-only after share sale news.</title>
<headline>Tosok bid-only after share sale news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of car parts maker Tosok Corp were bid-only on Tuesday morning after Nissan Motor Co Ltd announced that it had agreed to sell 3.67 million shares, or a 30 percent stake, of Tosok to Nippon Densan Corp.  </p>
<p>By 0025 GMT, Tosok's shares were bid-only at 605 yen.</p>
<p>They closed at 559 yen on Monday.</p>
<p>Nissan said on Monday it had agreed to sell 3.67 million shares of Tosok to Nippon Densan for about two billion yen at the end of March.</p>
<p>Nissan now owns 49 percent of Tosok, which makes automobile parts, such as power-steering and automatic transmission components.</p>
</text>
